# core/data/talk/grammar/en/rest_gesture.tlk - replies to gestures: a wave, a nod, a shake of the
# head, a hug, a gift, walking away, a high five (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-OPEN). Clean in any
# room, no register word, no romance. A hug is a plain hug: a child may decline, and an adult may
# too (a stranger, a rival). Rule names start with r_. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- WAVE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.wave.r_back act: wave
  "[HAPPY]Hi! *waves back* It's a good wave. We nailed it."
  "*waves* Hello! I did a big one. Did you see?"
  "Oh, a wave! *waves* Is it the same wave? It feels the same."
@rule core.wave.r_greet act: greet
  "Hello! A wave is the best hello. Silent, tidy, friendly."
  "Hi there! I'm waving, can you tell? I'm trying my best."
@rule core.wave.r_nod act: nod
  "*gives a small nod and a smaller wave*"
@rule core.wave.r_joke act: joke
  "I'd wave back, but my arm's asleep. Hold on, I'll wake it."
  "Was that a wave, or are you swatting a fly? Either way, hi."
@rule core.wave.r_morning guard: time=morning act: greet
  "Morning wave! Those are the best. Nobody's grumpy yet."
@rule core.wave.r_night guard: time=night act: greet
  "A midnight wave! Shh, hi. Everything's asleep."
@rule core.wave.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: wave
  "[HAPPY]Hi! *jumps and waves* Did you see me jump? I jumped!"
  "*waves with the whole body* Hello! I'm a windmill!"
@rule core.wave.r_flat guard: flat act: wave
  "*lifts one finger* That was my wave. It took effort."
@rule core.wave.r_loud guard: loud act: greet
  "HI! I SEE YOUR WAVE! HERE'S MINE! *WAVES VERY LARGE*"

# ---- NOD and SHAKE_HEAD --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.nod.r_back act: nod
  "*nods slowly* Yes. Deep. We understand each other."
  "*nods* Mm. That's the spirit."
@rule core.nod.r_back2 act: backchannel
  "Mm-hm! Exactly. I knew you'd see it."
  "Yeah? You nod, I nod. That's how it works."
@rule core.nod.r_tell act: tell
  "Right, good. Now, where was I? Something about toast."
  "You're nodding at the right bit. Very good."
@rule core.nod.r_joke act: joke
  "A nod! The sign of an expert, or a sleeper. Hard to tell."
@rule core.nod.r_cont act: continue
  "Okay, since you nodded, I'll go on. Don't blame me."
@rule core.nod.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: nod
  "*nods super fast* Yes! Yes yes yes!"
@rule core.shake_head.r_disagree act: disagree
  "No? You don't think so? Why not, I'm very open."
  "Aww, you're shaking your head. I wasn't done being right."
@rule core.shake_head.r_repeat act: ask_repeat
  "Wait, no to what? Back up. I lost the thread."
  "Hm? Was that a no, or a bug? I can't tell."
@rule core.shake_head.r_joke act: joke
  "Shake it off, shake it all off! Is it a dance? It's a dance."
  "That's the head-shake of a champion. Or a wet dog."
@rule core.shake_head.r_complain act: complain
  "Oh, great, a no. I didn't even finish asking."
@rule core.shake_head.r_agree act: agree
  "No, right, I agree. Not that, never that."
@rule core.shake_head.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "No?! Why no? I wanted a big yes!"

# ---- HUG: a plain hug, free to decline ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.hug.r_yes guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "[HAPPY]Aww, a hug! Come here, you. Mind the elbow."
  "A hug? Yes, please. I've been needing one."
  "Oh, bless. Okay, hug accepted. A good one."
@rule core.hug.r_thank guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: thank
  "Thank you. I really needed that. It's been a day."
  "That was lovely. You give excellent hugs."
@rule core.hug.r_joke guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: joke
  "A hug? Hold on, I'll brace. Okay, hit me gently."
  "I hug, you hug, we all hug. That's the whole town motto."
@rule core.hug.r_laugh guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: laugh
  "Ha! Okay, okay, just one. Maybe two, or four."
@rule core.hug.r_stranger guard: !kid_speaker&rel=stranger act: no
  "Oh! Um, I don't know you yet. A handshake, maybe?"
  "That's sweet, but I'm not a hugger with new people. Sorry."
@rule core.hug.r_stranger2 guard: !kid_speaker&rel=stranger act: joke
  "A hug, from a stranger! Bold. Let's start with hello."
@rule core.hug.r_rival guard: !kid_speaker&rel=rival act: dismiss
  "No, thank you. I'll hug you when the sun's a cucumber."
  "Hug? From you? Let's not, I'm busy being cross."
@rule core.hug.r_kid_yes guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: hug
  "[HAPPY]Hug! A big one! You're the squishiest!"
  "Okay! Hug! But no tickling, or a little tickling."
@rule core.hug.r_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: thank
  "Thanks! I needed a hug, and a snack. Do you have a snack?"
@rule core.hug.r_kid_laugh guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: laugh
  "Hee hee! You hugged me! You're my favourite."
@rule core.hug.r_kid_no guard: kid_speaker&rel=stranger tags: kid act: no
  "No, thank you. I'm shy. Can we wave instead?"
  "Um, no. I don't hug people I just met. Do you like cats?"
@rule core.hug.r_kid_no2 guard: kid_speaker&rel=stranger tags: kid act: dismiss
  "Nope, not now. You can wave, waving is great."
@rule core.hug.r_flat guard: flat&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Oh, a hug. {.}I'm hugging, this is my hugging face."
@rule core.hug.r_elder guard: elder&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Oh, dear, how kind. Come here. Mind my back."
@rule core.hug.r_blunt guard: blunt&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Fine. One hug. Don't make it a thing."
@rule core.hug.r_sad guard: mood=sad&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "[SAD]Oh. Thank you. I needed that more than I knew."
@rule core.hug.r_angry guard: mood=angry&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger act: dismiss
  "[ANGRY]Not now. I'm still hot. Give me a minute."

# ---- GIVE: a gift ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.give.r_thank act: thank
  "Oh, for me? Thank you, it's lovely. It's very something."
  "A gift! I'm touched, and I'll treasure it. Or put it on a shelf."
  "You shouldn't have! But I'm so glad you did."
  "Aww, thank you. I'll find a special place for it. Near the cat."
@rule core.give.r_joke act: joke
  "Is it a trap? It's a nice trap. I'll take it anyway."
  "A present! Quick, I need to hide it before the others see."
@rule core.give.r_pos act: opine_pos
  "I love it! It's exactly what I didn't know I wanted."
  "I'll use it every day. Or every other day. It's too nice."
@rule core.give.r_neg act: opine_neg
  "Hmm, it's interesting. I'm not sure what to do with it."
  "Oh, a thing. I'll put it somewhere far away."
@rule core.give.r_topic_pos guard: stance=pro&topic act: opine_pos
  "{x:cap}! You remembered. That's exactly my taste."
@rule core.give.r_topic_neg guard: stance=con&topic act: opine_neg
  "Oh, {x}. I'll be polite. It's the thought that counts, right?"
@rule core.give.r_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "How very kind. I shall treasure it, I assure you."
@rule core.give.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Wow! For me? Thank you, can I show everyone?"
  "A present! Thank you! I'll give you a rock in return."
@rule core.give.r_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Oh, you shouldn't have, dear. I'll keep it forever, or until tea."

# ---- WALK_AWAY: the player leaves mid-chat -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.walk_away.r_bye act: farewell
  "Oh, leaving? Okay, bye. I'll wave at your back."
  "Off you go, then. Come back when you're ready. No rush."
  "Bye! Thanks for stopping by. Even if it was brief."
@rule core.walk_away.r_complain act: complain
  "Hey, rude! I was mid-sentence, in the middle of a good one."
  "Well, that's how it's going to be? Fine. Whatever."
@rule core.walk_away.r_joke act: joke
  "And with that, the visitor vanished! Into the fog. Dramatic."
  "Bye! Don't mind me, I'll finish my story to the wall."
@rule core.walk_away.r_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Fine. Go. I didn't need that conversation anyway."
@rule core.walk_away.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Hey! Wait, I wasn't done, come back!"
@rule core.walk_away.r_polite guard: polite act: farewell
  "Oh, well. Do take care, then. Another time, perhaps."

# ---- HIGH_FIVE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.high_five.r_back act: high_five
  "[HAPPY]Up high! {.}Yes! That was a good one!"
  "High five! Slap! Ow, worth it."
  "Boom! Nailed it. We should do this for a living."
  "Yes! Give me five, give me ten, give me a snack!"
@rule core.high_five.r_laugh act: laugh
  "Ha! That was a loud one. Everyone heard."
  "Heh. My hand's going to be red. I regret nothing."
@rule core.high_five.r_joke act: joke
  "High five accepted. Please keep your hands to the snacks."
  "Up top! Or low, or sideways. I'm flexible."
@rule core.high_five.r_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Not now, my hand's busy. Maybe later."
@rule core.high_five.r_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: high_five
  "High five! Down low, too slow! Again, again!"
  "Yes! Five! Gimme another, behind the back!"
@rule core.high_five.r_loud guard: loud act: high_five
  "HIGH FIVE! SLAP! OUCH, AGAIN!"
@rule core.high_five.r_polite guard: polite act: high_five
  "Ah, a high five! Splendid. I do enjoy a firm clap."
@rule core.high_five.r_elder guard: elder act: laugh
  "Ha! At my age? Fine, but gently, my wrist's a window."
